WEBVTT

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:07.900
You must only kill your enemy
after making them regret ever becoming your enemy.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.990
Yes, I will let you live.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.120
You will soon pray for the arrival of the Imperial forces.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.330
Who said you were allowed to defend yourself?

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.710
Do you want to protect yourself or the hostages?

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.840
If you care about the hostages,
then you will keep your hands on the ground.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.600
I'm counting on you, Iskender.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.440
The Council of Generals

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.420
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.410
Hey, Imperial!

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.740
Were you lying about making this city our nation?!

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.460
Was it true what that man said
about the Empire tricking us?!

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.510
That little boy has certainly caused
enough trouble for us.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.760
We're returning to the tent.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.430
Hey, not so fast! You told us
you would make our dreams come true.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.260
Was that promise you made to us a lie?! Tell us now!

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.890
Shut up.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:53.020
If you don't shut your mouths, I'll set fire to the tent
and burn the Torqye hostages alive.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.780
Then you'll spend the rest of your lives being hunted
by Torqye until they kill every last one of you.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.410
What is that commotion in the plaza?

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.330
Once the Imperial army arrives,

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.580
we have to fight on their side.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.920
Then the Empire will release the hostages.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:23.050
All we can do is trust
that the Empire will keep its promise.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.390
Keep the siege towers on standby!
I want them ready to attack.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.150
I didn't want to have to resort to this.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:44.910
But with only 4000 soldiers, there is no other way for us
to stop the 40,000 Araba tribesmen marching towards us.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:49.370
Pasha, you're not thinking of using poison, are you?

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.410
What do I do?

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.510
Don't you think we've waited long enough?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.550
Yes, perhaps it's time I took care of this.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.020
Make it flashy while you're at it.
I need to alleviate this boredom.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.730
What are you doing?!

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.400
Nobody intervene!

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:22.900
You bastards!

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.160
Even so...

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.660
Listen, when I draw their attention,

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.130
I need you to cut as many ropes from the tent
as you can.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:42.470
What exactly is he planning to do?

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.840
Actually, what's that weird smell coming from the tent?

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.890
Okay, that's far enough.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.520
So could you tell me
what you're doing here, Miss Dancer?

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.360
He was tougher than he looked.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:06.570
I'd expect nothing less from Minister Louis' Rod Orm.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:11.370
Somebody help treat Glalat!
We're leaving once that's done!

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:16.170
I'm done waiting around for Louis' gambit.
We'll take Hisar ourselves!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.130
I think it's time we do things our way!

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.720
I almost feel sorry for you.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.300
Being in the military at your young age,

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.970
you must have worked hard to get to where you are.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:35.140
And because you prioritized
your personal feelings for a fool like Ibrahim Vali,

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.270
it all came to nothing.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.980
You can contemplate
just where you went wrong with your life,

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:45.030
as you fight through the pain and regret.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.740
Since the reason why you must die like this

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.120
is all because of him.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:57.080
I have never regretted being Ibrahim's friend!

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.590
Pain is merciless.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:07.340
Could you say that again after losing your arm?

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:13.850
Little lady, you must be with that boy from earlier.
Tell me who you are.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.320
What is going on?!

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.580
Thank you, Iskender.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.670
This is bad, the hostages are going to escape! The fire--

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.380
Stop! If you set it on fire now...

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:48.970
-Now!
-Run!

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.680
What?!

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:54.430
Everyone head for the plaza!
Have the guards open the gates!

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:58.770
Send a messenger to Zaganos immediately
and request his support in taking back the city!

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.230
Yes, sir!

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.020
Mahmut actually did it.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:10.030
Open the gate! Open the gate!

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.540
Ah, we're too late.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.380
What shall I do with this?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:27.710
Just apologize to Louis
and tell him you were drunk or something.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.550
All right, men, you can see the situation.
Start packing things up here.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.310
The expedition doesn't end
until we are back in the castle.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.890
Hurry up and go to Louis.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.520
No! I'm not going to go out of my way
to get myself killed!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.320
Then what are we going to do?!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:50.700
You know how crazy that minister can get
when he loses it.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:55.160
Well, we could make it look like he was crushed
by a boulder.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:59.200
Oh, that's a great idea! Yeah, let's go with that!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.080
Hurry up, everyone! I want us out of here by nightfall!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.000
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.090
Now you've done it.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:30.480
I'll say this for your benefit,
but that man is not worth saving.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:34.820
He prioritized his own personal feelings
over his duty as Vali.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.820
He has failed as Vali.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.220
Ibrahim.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:05.060
You have not failed as Vali.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:08.810
I believe a person who prioritizes the lives of hostages

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.400
over trying to stop a rebellion

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.070
is just the kind of person

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:16.070
I want as Vali.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.870
No matter what anybody says.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.830
Someone like you...

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.290
should be Vali.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:34.420
The Divan, the highest authority in all of Torqye.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:39.100
The most important aspect of these meetings

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:43.470
is that all decisions require
the unanimous support of all 13 Pashas.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:49.020
It is a council that handles matters of the military,
diplomacy and treason.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:56.400
I hereby call to order this Divan
regarding the rebellion in Hisar.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:01.780
If you wish to defend yourself to the council
in regards to the part you played,

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:05.160
leading your forces of a thousand men to take up arms,

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:08.170
now is your chance.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.960
It is as I testified yesterday.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:16.170
My only choices were to either watch them burn
the hostages alive, or help the Empire.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.970
Leading my thousand men as Vali,

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:24.430
I chose to prioritize the lives of their families
who were taken hostage.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:30.560
Why did you leave Hisar during the festival to visit Altin?

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:34.860
All Binbashis of the First Province were gathering
in the capital,

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:40.530
so Zaganos Pasha organized a meeting
in order to share information.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:47.120
Zehir Zaganos Pasha. Is this true?

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:52.290
Yes, I can only blame my own carelessness
regarding that matter.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.540
What?!

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:55.710
Mahmut Pasha...

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.590
you were not given permission to speak.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.010
Moving on.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.350
Tughril Mahmut Pasha.

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:08.100
Explain to the council the decision you made
after the rebellion had been quelled,

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.770
concerning the Araba people.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.780
Release the Araba?

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.530
You're not serious, are you?

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:22.700
They freely admitted to attacking this city.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.830
If they are not punished for this,

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:30.040
then it would be the same as telling the neighboring
countries that Torqye is a nation of weaklings.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.290
I am aware of that.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:38.420
However, the only people who will be able to convince
the 40,000 Arabans out there to return to Empire territory

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:44.430
are these people
who know that the Empire deceived them.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:12:01.400
I, Mahmut the Golden Eagle,
hereby release you all.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.940
Thank you, Shara.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.320
You're welcome.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:50.120
There was no reason to release all of them.
Did that not occur to you?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.450
Not at all.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:56.460
The nomadic Araba people gathered together
in the hopes that their prayers had been answered.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:01.510
There is no telling what they would do
if we harmed one of them.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:06.470
If by some chance, fighting should break out
and harm unarmed Araba,

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.220
that would surely draw the ire of neighboring countries

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.430
and give the Empire the chance to strike.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:17.860
That concludes our questions.
We will now enter deliberations.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.580
And that's the end of that!

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.210
I really have to thank you, Mahmut.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:45.170
-You'll stay in Hisar tonight, won't you?
-Yes, I think I will.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:49.090
Good! Then you're staying with me!
We'll stay up all night--

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.430
Is this fun? It is fun, isn't it?

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:58.060
I'll play with you both as much as you want tonight.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:04.320
After all, my head might not be attached
to my body by this time next week.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:10.530
To the Divan, all acts of rebellion
against the Stratocracy are punishable by death.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.830
There is nothing I can do now.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.870
I hereby reconvene the Divan.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:23.050
Ibrahim Vali, step forward.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:29.340
If I find out that you framed Ibrahim,

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.720
I'll never forgive you.

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:34.970
Hold your tongue, Mahmut Pasha.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.100
We are in the middle of the Divan.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:43.940
Let the records show that you, Ibrahim Vali,
shall be reinstated as Vali of Hisar.

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:48.200
Ibrahim Vali, take a seat on the third floor.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:52.320
Zehir Zaganos Pasha, please step forward.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:05.630
Did you do something for me?

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:08.090
No, but...

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:14.140
-I'm glad.
-Thank you.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.890
But why?

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:23.150
The fact remains that Ibrahim's actions were crimes
against the nation.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:28.650
Let the records show that you,
Zehir Zaganos Pasha, shall be reinstated as Pasha.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:33.120
Zehir Zaganos Pasha, please join the other pashas.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:37.870
Tughril Mahmut Pasha, please step forward.

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:43.210
It's clear these judgments are not impartial.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.670
By questioning Ibrahim's crime,

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:52.260
the Divan would be able to clear Zaganos Pasha
of his crimes as well.

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:56.510
Could it be that they're not punishing
these two men in such important positions

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:59.560
because war is near?

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:04.860
Let the records show that you, Tughril Mahmut Pasha,
shall be stripped of your title of Pasha.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.110
Why?!

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:18.370
Why?! The reason why Hisar was saved,
the reason the hostages were rescued,

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.330
it was all because of him, wasn't it?!

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:28.500
Your new position shall be Binbashi,
serving under the Seventh Province's Halil Pasha.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:32.260
The duration of this punishment is indefinite.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:38.850
Why?

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:44.350
Are you asking why you were removed as Pasha?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:45.560
Yes.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:52.530
Well, why did you become Pasha?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:56.450
Because I did not want war to break out somewhere

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.030
and lose somebody close to me.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:04.000
Then how do you think
we can achieve that as a country?

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:09.590
Mahmut, the Pasha's job is to think of these things.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:14.380
Going to rescue a friend in need is truly
a wonderful and noble act.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:18.100
But that is not a Pasha's first priority.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.310
This latest matter was also a threat to Torqye,

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:27.100
but when you rushed out to save Ibrahim,
you forgot you were Pasha, didn't you?

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:31.570
That is a much more serious mistake
than you think it is.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:41.290
Your rank was taken from you
because you have much to learn as Pasha.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:47.120
It would be better for you to meet more people
and see more sights.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.790
Then you can come back.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.210
Halil Pasha is right.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:56.550
I've been acting as an individual.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:02.760
Despite my responsibilities as Pasha,
I acted without any thought.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.770
I have no right to call myself Pasha.

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:08.850
Please, wait.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:14.320
Is Torqye preparing to start a war?

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:22.280
I cannot answer that, as you are no longer Pasha.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:39.220
At this crucial time, when war could break out,

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.390
I cannot be in the position to make decisions.

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:44.260
This is the worst.

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:58.320
If Hisar's gates hadn't opened when they did,
I wouldn't have been able to do anything.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:02.070
I had thought and planned for months,

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.240
only to make a crucial mistake in the end.

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:09.500
And as a result, I was saved by a boy
who acted out of emotion.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.670
But this time was merely a coincidence.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:16.460
It's not because your actions were correct
that everything happened to work out.

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:25.060
This is the means to contact the spies
I've sent out across the continent.

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:28.270
It's the reason
I knew of the Empire's movements beforehand.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.520
Take it.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.520
I knew it! So you are--!

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.320
The threat of the Empire is approaching.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:40.030
In order to prove it, Zaganos Pasha was willing
to use Hisar as a warning.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:44.240
And the Divan, who were vaguely aware of what he did,

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:47.580
reinstated Zaganos Pasha because of his capabilities.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.750
This was the world I tried to take on.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.750
I was never thinking about Torqye as a whole.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:59.720
And yet I blindly believed I was right.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.760
Everything I did was for myself.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:06.680
I was so wrong.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.480
I graciously accept.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:41.130
This time, I will return
as someone worthy of being Pasha.

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:46.220
I will come back.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:01.650
It seems the cold temperatures persist, Glalat.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:06.070
Yes. Despite it being spring,
there have been some who have frozen to death.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:13.080
If you so desire, I would be happy to have supplies sent
to Ellvaldesberg from Imperial territory.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.040
We don't need your charity.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:24.260
More importantly,
we want to get out and spread our wings.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:30.350
You are as demanding as ever.
I will not make the same mistake twice.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:36.850
You're still planning on using those useless Rod Orms?

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:42.280
The reason Zaganos Pasha beat us to Hisar...

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:48.530
it was because of the spy network
he's established across the continent.

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:51.620
-Spy network?
-You have nothing to worry about.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:56.620
I am in the process of using the Rod Orm to root it out.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:02.630
Zaganos Pasha will lose his precious eyes and ears.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:06.880
Glalat.

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:16.600
It looks like we won't have to fear the cold this winter.

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:53.240
I must return to my hometown
to search for what I need.

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:56.120
Black Eagle? Who are you?

00:23:56.530 --> 00:23:58.540
Next episode, "The Eagle's Joint Struggle."

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:01.790
The voice in my heart will shed light on my path.
